---
import Section from '../../../components/ui/Section.astro';
---

<Section class="experience" id="experience" labelledBy="experience-title">
  <div class="section-topline"><span class="index">03 / EXPERIENCE</span><span class="label">Internships</span></div>
  <div class="experience-heading">
    <h2 id="experience-title">Experience<span>.</span></h2>
    <p>My work in product and software engineering, from investigating customer issues to building practical tools.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="experience-list">
    <article class="experience-entry">
      <div class="experience-entry__meta"><span>01 / PRODUCT ENGINEERING</span><span>JUN 2026 — AUG 2026</span></div>
      <div class="experience-entry__body">
        <div><h3>Fin from<br />Salesforce<span class="experience-dot">.</span></h3><p class="experience-role">Product Engineering Intern</p></div>
        <div class="experience-copy"><p>Worked on Fin Messenger, investigating customer issues across the web product and mobile, tracing problems through a large production codebase and carefully testing fixes.</p><p>Built a feature that automatically turns off time-sensitive notices after a set period. Working on a production product gave me first-hand experience of debugging, collaboration and making changes for real users.</p><div class="experience-keywords"><span>Product engineering</span><span>Debugging</span><span>Collaboration</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="experience-entry">
      <div class="experience-entry__meta"><span>02 / SOFTWARE ENGINEERING</span><span>JUN 2025 — DEC 2025</span></div>
      <div class="experience-entry__body">
        <div><h3>Cloudcards<span class="experience-dot">.</span></h3><p class="experience-role">Software Engineering Intern</p></div>
        <div class="experience-copy"><p>Helped build a desktop application for uploading large aviation datasets, making a complex process easier to manage with pause, resume and progress tracking.</p><p>Worked closely with the operations team to understand their workflow and shape the application around the way they work. It was a chance to help build a practical tool from the beginning and see it used in a real working environment.</p><div class="experience-keywords"><span>Desktop development</span><span>Product thinking</span><span>User workflows</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div></Section>
